d{aligned}],\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ in terms of the components of $y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066712/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a58bdf4310a132c712eaafc313f29c50f97c6ca5c7e4934f0f05f948cf5f825"} {"question" "q-94153" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})^{2}+(-{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}+{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{y}_{1}^{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066712/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a58bdf4310a132c712eaafc313f29c50f97c6ca5c7e4934f0f05f948cf5f825"} {"question" "q-94153" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cd4afffd6d08f8c6a1c33a4fcbb5d3b4ed311a04ddb22e906a1ce299eba2fb26"} {"question" "q-94153" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066712/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a58bdf4310a132c712eaafc313f29c50f97c6ca5c7e4934f0f05f948cf5f825"} {"question" "q